"level":4},{"id":"deprecated","text":"Deprecated","level":4},{"id":"setstate","text":"setState()","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"state","text":"state","level":5},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"deprecated-2","text":"Deprecated","level":4},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tdata","text":"TData","level":3},{"id":"deprecated-3","text":"Deprecated","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# ~~Type Alias: LegacyReactTable\\<TData\\>~~\n\n```ts\ntype LegacyReactTable<TData> = ReactTable<LegacyFeatures, TData, TableState<LegacyFeatures>> & object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [react-table/src/useLegacyTable.ts:290](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/react-table/src/useLegacyTable.ts#L290)\n\nLegacy table instance type that includes the v8-style `getState()` method.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### ~~getState()~~\n\n```ts\ngetState: () => TableState<LegacyFeatures>;\n```\n\nReturns the current table state.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`TableState`\\<[`LegacyFeatures`](../interfaces/LegacyFeatures.md)\\>\n\n#### Deprecated\n\nIn v9, access state directly via `table.state` or use `table.state` for the full state.\n\n### ~~setState()~~\n\n```ts\nsetState: (state) => void;\n```\n\nSets the current table state.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### state\n\n`TableState`\\<[`LegacyFeatures`](../interfaces/LegacyFeatures.md)\\>\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### Deprecated\n\nIn v9, access state directly via `table.baseAtoms`\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` *extends* `RowData`\n\n## Deprecated\n\nUse `useTable` with explicit state selection instead.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: LegacyReactTable\ntitle: LegacyReactTable\n---\n\n# ~~Type Alias: LegacyReactTable\\<TData\\>~~\n\n```ts\ntype LegacyReactTable<TData> = ReactTable<LegacyFeatures, TData, TableState<LegacyFeatures>> & object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [react-table/src/useLegacyTable.ts:290](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/react-table/src/useLegacyTable.ts#L290)\n\nLegacy table instance type that includes the v8-style `getState()` method.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### ~~getState()~~\n\n```ts\ngetState: () => TableState<LegacyFeatures>;\n```\n\nReturns the current table state.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`TableState`\\<[`LegacyFeatures`](../interfaces/LegacyFeatures.md)\\>\n\n#### Deprecated\n\nIn v9, access state directly via `table.state` or use `table.state` for the full state.\n\n### ~~setState()~~\n\n```ts\nsetState: (state) => void;\n```\n\nSets the current table state.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### state\n\n`TableState`\\<[`LegacyFeatures`](../interfaces/LegacyFeatures.md)\\>\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### Deprecated\n\nIn v9, access state directly via `table.baseAtoms`\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` *extends* `RowData`\n\n## Deprecated\n\nUse `useTable` with explicit state selection instead.\n"}
